    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0785" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/394: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-14T10:00:00+01:00">July 14, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 14—7:17 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Department’s 22, July 13, 5 p.m. Will discuss convention with Wilson in Berne
                    today. Text was finally approved yesterday and signed by the following 28
                    countries: Austria, Belgium, Bolivia, Canada, Chile, Costa Rica, Cuba,
                    Czechoslovakia, Denmark, Ethiopia, France, Germany, Great Britain, Guatemala,
                    Hejaz, India, Italy, Japan, Mexico, The Netherlands, Panama, Paraguay, Portugal,
                    San Marino, Siam, Switzerland, Uruguay, Venezuela.</p>
                <p>Several other countries including Egypt and the Argentine anticipate signing
                    today.</p>
                <p>Am telegraphing full text of the convention in clear with the exception of
                    chemical formulae. Summary of the final act and protocol of signature being
                        telegraphed.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d533-f1"/> Full text of these will only be
                    telegraphed if Department instructs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d533-f1" n="9" xml:id="d533-f1-content">
                <p>Telegrams not printed. For texts of convention and protocol of signature, see
                        <ref target="#pg675">p. 675</ref>; for text of final act, see League of
                    Nations document C.455(c).M.193(c).1931.XI (Geneva, August 26, 1931). Texts are
                    also printed in Department of State Conference Series No. 10, pp. 27 ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
